1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,217
Last time the Corsair Queen was the Warlord with a new name.

2
00:00:05,667 --> 00:00:09,146
She flew a Kralien dreadnought, with Kralien escorts.

3
00:00:09,596 --> 00:00:12,639
This is the same file after today.

4
00:00:13,089 --> 00:00:20,480
She arrives when I say, in the ships I chose, with the fleets I chose. Six lines.

5
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:24,289
Here is where we left her.

6
00:00:24,739 --> 00:00:28,652
Everything today is between Boss and the closing fence.

7
00:00:29,102 --> 00:00:30,841
Trigger and Low: when.

8
00:00:31,291 --> 00:00:34,335
Flies and Fleets: what comes with her.

9
00:00:34,785 --> 00:00:36,089
Difficulty: how big.

10
00:00:36,539 --> 00:00:38,278
Named: her own ships.

11
00:00:38,728 --> 00:00:43,946
We will change them one at a time, and play after each.

12
00:00:45,146 --> 00:00:47,754
First, make her easy to test.

13
00:00:48,204 --> 00:00:52,987
Low is the share of raiders still flying when she arrives.

14
00:00:53,437 --> 00:00:58,654
One hundred percent means all of them, so she arrives at once.

15
00:00:59,104 --> 00:01:02,148
Four seconds in, and there she is.

16
00:01:02,598 --> 00:01:06,946
We will put a real number back at the end.

17
00:01:08,146 --> 00:01:09,885
Trigger has two values.

18
00:01:10,335 --> 00:01:14,248
Enemies low: one arrival, when the raiders thin out.

19
00:01:14,698 --> 00:01:21,220
Continuous: no arrival at all, just a new wave every so many seconds, all game.

20
00:01:21,670 --> 00:01:31,235
They are different kinds of boss, and a continuous boss ignores half of this file: no named ship, no objective, no Low.

21
00:01:31,685 --> 00:01:33,859
The page has a table.

22
00:01:34,309 --> 00:01:36,483
We stay with enemies low.

23
00:01:36,933 --> 00:01:43,454
One warning: if you misspell this word, the boss never comes, and nothing tells you.

24
00:01:44,654 --> 00:01:50,741
Low is a share of the largest number of raiders the game has seen.

25
00:01:51,191 --> 00:01:54,670
With twenty raiders, twenty-five percent is five left.

26
00:01:55,120 --> 00:01:56,859
Forty percent is eight.

27
00:01:57,309 --> 00:01:59,483
Always type the percent sign.

28
00:01:59,933 --> 00:02:06,454
Without it, forty means forty times the raiders, and she is there at the start.

29
00:02:06,904 --> 00:02:13,426
And the game looks every four seconds, so she is never exactly on the kill.

30
00:02:14,626 --> 00:02:18,539
Fleets is how many escort fleets come with her.

31
00:02:18,989 --> 00:02:21,598
A whole number, as a digit.

32
00:02:22,048 --> 00:02:26,396
Zero, or no line at all, and she comes alone.

33
00:02:26,846 --> 00:02:32,063
How many ships are in a fleet is not on this line.

34
00:02:32,513 --> 00:02:34,687
That is the next two.

35
00:02:35,887 --> 00:02:38,496
Flies is who flies the fleets.

36
00:02:38,946 --> 00:02:42,859
Six races can: Kralien, Torgoth, Arvonian, Skaraan, Ximni, Pirate.

37
00:02:43,309 --> 00:02:46,787
One race, and every fleet is that race.

38
00:02:47,237 --> 00:02:52,454
Or a mix, with a percent on each and a comma between.

39
00:02:53,654 --> 00:02:57,567
The crew picks the game's difficulty, one to eleven.

40
00:02:58,017 --> 00:03:01,930
Plus two means two levels above whatever they picked.

41
00:03:02,380 --> 00:03:05,424
A bare number means that level, always.

42
00:03:05,874 --> 00:03:09,352
The level sets the size of each fleet.

43
00:03:09,802 --> 00:03:14,585
At level seven a pirate fleet is one to three ships.

44
00:03:15,035 --> 00:03:18,078
A Kralien fleet is four to six.

45
00:03:18,528 --> 00:03:20,702
At eleven, everything is six.

46
00:03:21,152 --> 00:03:24,196
Difficulty does not touch her named ships.

47
00:03:25,396 --> 00:03:27,570
Named is her own ships.

48
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:29,759
Name, then ship key.

49
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:34,557
You know the first rule: the name is one word.

50
00:03:35,007 --> 00:03:39,789
The key comes from this table, typed exactly, lowercase with underscores.

51
00:03:40,239 --> 00:03:43,283
A second ship goes after a comma.

52
00:03:43,733 --> 00:03:49,385
A corsair queen in a pirate brigantine, and her second in a strongbow.

53
00:03:50,585 --> 00:03:51,889
Lint first. Clean.

54
00:03:52,339 --> 00:03:55,383
Lint reads the shape of a line.

55
00:03:55,833 --> 00:03:58,876
Misspell the label, and it tells you.

56
00:03:59,326 --> 00:04:04,543
But it does not check what comes after the colon. Pirates, plural.

57
00:04:04,993 --> 00:04:06,298
Lint says clean.

58
00:04:06,748 --> 00:04:14,139
And in the game, the Queen arrives with no fleets at all, and nothing is written anywhere.

59
00:04:14,589 --> 00:04:16,763
So after lint, play it.

60
00:04:17,213 --> 00:04:21,996
The page has the whole list of what lint cannot see.

61
00:04:22,446 --> 00:04:33,750
Two of them stop the game on an error page: a word where Low wants a number, and a word after the plus sign on Difficulty.

62
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,254
Testing is over.

63
00:04:36,704 --> 00:04:41,922
Forty percent: the crew is winning, and the siege is not over.

64
00:04:42,372 --> 00:04:51,067
And I bring the note up to date, because in a year I will not remember what plus two meant.

65
00:04:52,267 --> 00:04:54,007
Now your own boss.

66
00:04:54,457 --> 00:05:02,283
Give it a race that fits its story, its own ships, and an arrival you chose on purpose.

67
00:05:02,733 --> 00:05:06,646
Then make a wave boss in a second file.

68
00:05:07,096 --> 00:05:08,835
Next time: the objective.
